Subject: [PATCH] geolocation: a switch serves the profile location

--fingerprint-geolocation=<lat>,<lon>[,<accuracy_m>] makes
navigator.geolocation answer with the given position, so a page that
holds the geolocation permission reads the profile's location and not
the host's. A fixed location provider is then the only provider: no
platform provider (CoreLocation, WinRT, the Linux portal) and no network
provider is ever created, so no Wi-Fi scan and no request to a location
service leaves the machine. On Windows and macOS the system location
source reports the permission as allowed and never touches the
operating system's location settings or services.

The site permission prompt stays as it is. After the page is granted,
the first fix arrives 400 to 1200 ms later, as from a real provider,
with the current time as its timestamp. Altitude, altitude accuracy,
heading and speed stay unset, so a page reads them as null. The
accuracy defaults to 50 metres. watchPosition gets the one fix, as from
a device that does not move. A value that does not parse, or is out of
range, gives POSITION_UNAVAILABLE and never the host's location.

Without the switch nothing changes.

